[I] A minimal http/ftp download tool for boot disks

[T] fget by Felix von Leitner downloads a single HTTP or FTP URL and writes
[T] the file to stdout. It is very small, supports IPv4 and IPv6 and the
[T] http_proxy and ftp_proxy variables, which makes it suitable for boot
[T] disks.

[A] Felix von Leitner <felix-fget@fefe.de>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/network
[F] CROSS DIETLIBC NO-LTO

[L] GPL
[V] 0.4.1

[D] dfb6caa889fabb8d60df741f87473c6e72bfc0223fd477edd286165b fget-0.4.1.tar.bz2 http://www.fefe.de/fget/

var_append CC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' -std=gnu17

hook_add premake 5 "echo $CC > conf-cc; echo $CC > conf-ld"
var_append makeopt ' ' fget

makeinstopt=
hook_add postmake 5 "install fget $root$bindir/"
